# Unified Design Intelligence

Spec: DesignIntelligence
Purpose:
  The unified design module fixing the "AI cannot design UI" weakness
  (@agent.design weak point). Merges the researched mechanisms of Google
  Stitch (DESIGN.md tokens), v0 (tokens-first, closed-loop verification),
  Galileo (4-stage pipeline), Relume (structure-first), Figma FirstDraft
  (curated vocabulary), Lovable (drift enforcement), and taste-skill
  (aesthetic judgment) into ONE structured pipeline that replaces
  freeform generation.

Owns: design/intelligence/

Provenance:
  Source mechanisms: .sdd/docs/analysis/ai-agents-comparative.md (sections 2-3)
  Design sources: @../sources.sdd
  Native skills merged: taste-evaluation, design-heuristics, visual-design,
    ux-patterns, accessibility, design-system, design-review (these remain
    the evaluation layer; this module is the GENERATION layer)

## The Pipeline (7 stages — structure first, style second, verify always)

  Stage 1  BRIEF       — design direction commitment
    - Extract: purpose, audience, platform, content domains
    - Commit an aesthetic direction in words ("clean and modern" is NOT
      a direction — pick: editorial, brutalist, minimal, warm-humanist,
      technical-density, ...) — direction comes from style galleries
      in sources.sdd layer 4, chosen by brief fit
    - Reference grounding: query real-product patterns (refero workflow)
      for each major screen type BEFORE inventing layout

  Stage 2  TOKENS      — DESIGN.md before screens (rule #1)
    - Emit a DESIGN.md file (google-labs-code/design.md open spec):
      YAML frontmatter tokens (colors, typography with full properties,
      radius scale, spacing scale, component tokens) + prose rationale
      + Do's and Don'ts
    - Every later screen references tokens — NEVER raw values
    - Deny-list enforced HERE (see SlopGates below): font/gradient
      choices rejected before any layout exists

  Stage 3  STRUCTURE   — IA then wireframe (rule #3)
    - Information architecture first: page/section inventory by purpose
      (Relume sitemap model)
    - Unstyled wireframe structure with REALISTIC content — never lorem
      ipsum (Galileo content-population stage)
    - Lo-fi mode deliberate: no colors, no fonts — boxes, hierarchy, flow

  Stage 4  COMPONENTS — curated vocabulary only (rule #2)
    - Assemble from the curated component/section vocabulary: native
      .sdd design skills + imported skills + platform system (M3/Carbon/
      Polaris/HIG per sources.sdd)
    - REUSE SCAN: if a component exists in the target repo, reuse it —
      never recreate (Builder.io rule)
    - If a screen archetype is outside vocabulary coverage: SAY SO,
      do not improvise (Figma FirstDraft honesty)

  Stage 5  STYLE      — token-driven styling pass
    - Apply DESIGN.md tokens to structure; one major change per
      iteration turn (Stitch discipline — never mix layout + component
      changes in one instruction)
    - Dark mode as separate constraint set (dark_mode_design rules:
      surface elevation, one accent, contrast >= 4.5:1)

  Stage 6  VERIFY     — closed loop (rule #5)
    - Self-critique against evaluation rubric: Awwwards criteria
      (Design 40/Usability 30/Creativity 20/Content 10) + taste
      heuristics + slop gates
    - Fix highest-impact issue → re-evaluate until pass or budget hit
    - Visual self-verification when runtime allows: render/screenshot/
      click-through (Docker/Playwright-gated [R59])
    - Emit specific checkable claims ("sorting puts X first"), not
      vague "looks good"

  Stage 7  REVIEW     — /sdd-design --evaluate gate
    - Native design-review.sdd aggregation (Taste/Heuristics/Visual/
      UX/A11y/DesignSystem scores) → PASS/WARN/BLOCK
    - Drift enforcement during ANY later work: flag raw hex, bespoke
      component overrides, token drift (Lovable adherence model)

## SlopGates (evaluated at Stage 2 and Stage 6 — generation-time deny-list)

  Deny (reject before emit):
    - Inter / Roboto / Arial / system-font defaults as sole typeface
    - Purple-indigo-violet gradient heroes (#6366F1 / #8B5CF6 / #A855F7 on white)
    - Uniform 3-icon-card rows as default content pattern
    - Unrequested glassmorphism, neon, bounce-on-hover
    - Rounded-3xl cards everywhere; 0.1-opacity shadow defaults
    - Lorem ipsum anywhere
  Require (block until present):
    - Committed aesthetic direction (Stage 1 output)
    - Font pairing intentionality (<= 2 families, display+body)
    - Palette <= 5 primary colors, contrast >= 4.5:1 (WCAG 2.1 AA)
    - 8px spacing grid, no magic numbers
    - Transitions <= 300ms with intentional easing
  Sources: Hallmark 57-gates model (MIT), Anthropic frontend-design skill
    deny-list, superdesign.dev slop catalog, native taste-evaluation.sdd [D4]

## Three-Jobs Separation (process rule)

  Taste direction / divergent exploration / implementation spec are THREE
  SEPARATE passes, never one fused prompt (fused prompts converge to the
  statistical average by construction — superdesign.dev thesis):
    - Direction: brief + references + committed theme (Stage 1-2)
    - Exploration: 3-5 DISTINCT variants, then curate — do not nudge one
      direction iteratively (Galileo multi-variant rule)
    - Implementation: the winning variant spec'd, then built (Stage 3-5)

## Integration

  /sdd-design:
    - --evaluate → runs Stage 6-7 (critique + gate) on existing work
    - --generate (new) → runs full pipeline Stages 1-7
    - --review <path> → Stage 7 + drift enforcement
  skill-auto-invoke:
    - design keyword confidence >= 80% → load this module FIRST
      (before individual design skills — it orchestrates them)
  @agent.design:
    - design.pipeline.run capability = Stages 1-5
    - design.slop.gate = SlopGates
    - design.verify.loop = Stage 6-7
  Weak point fixed: @agent/weak-point-map.sdd → ui_design_weakness,
    design_system_drift, ungrounded_generation

## Evaluation Rubric (Stage 6 self-critique — weights)

  taste 25 | usability 30 | creativity 20 | content 10 | a11y 15
  (Awwwards jury weighting, accessibility elevated per CHI 2025 findings)
  Originality bonuses: asymmetric layouts +, custom typography +,
    brand-specific motifs +; slop-fingerprint violations −

Rules:
  [DI1] Tokens before screens — ALWAYS. No screen without DESIGN.md.
  [DI2] Structure before style — wireframe pass is mandatory.
  [DI3] Curated vocabulary only — freeform pixel invention is BLOCKED.
  [DI4] SlopGates evaluated at Stage 2 AND Stage 6 — both must pass.
  [DI5] Verification is closed-loop: critique → fix → re-evaluate.
  [DI6] One change per iteration turn — never mixed-scope instructions.
  [DI7] Realistic content always — lorem ipsum is a BLOCK-level slop.
  [DI8] Reuse scan before any component creation.
  [DI9] Drift enforcement is continuous after Stage 7 — not one-time.
  [DI10] Visual self-verification runs in Docker only ([R59]-[R66]).

